{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>Torn.</b> By lion or wolf." "<b>I would bear it.</b> Language of one who slings a stone at the hair and does not miss (Judges 20), ״אֲנִי וּבְנִי שְׁלֹמֹה חַטָּאִים״ (I Kings 1) — defective; I would be responsible for it. If it was lacking, it was lacking from me — for from my hand you would demand it." "(<b>I would bear it.</b> Its Targum is דַּהֲוַת שָׁגְיָא מִמִּנְיָנָא — that it would be in excess of the count: it would be checked and found short, like ״וְלֹא נִפְקַד מִמֶּנּוּ אִישׁ״ (Numbers 31), whose Targum is לָא שְׁגָא.)" "<b>I was stolen from by day and I was stolen from by night.</b> Theft of day or theft of night — I paid for all." "<b>I was stolen from.</b> Like ״רַבִּיתִי בַגּוֹיִם שָׂרַתִּי בַּמְּדִינוֹת״ (Lamentations 1), ״מְלֵאֲתִי מִשְׁפָּט״ (Isaiah 1), ״אָהַבְתִּי לָדוּשׁ״ (Hosea 10)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:36.987457511Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}